id: pm-linear-field-ownership
title: Preview Linear field ownership and same-field conflicts
description: Compare an explicitly acknowledged Linear field snapshot with complete SDK local reads and current provider observations. Read-only preview; no cross-system atomic guarantee.
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-27T09:23:36.129Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T12:47:19.351Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Disjoint edits are distinguished from same-field conflicts; unknown bases never imply safe overwrites; preview makes zero mutations and explicitly declines atomic cross-system guarantees; typed SDK and CLI, compact TOON/JSON, actionable refusals, docs, seeded model tests and public tracker validation."
comments[15]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T09:23:55.309Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked: host SDK exposes threeWayFieldConflict and complete SDK reads; Linear negotiateLinearSchema detects metadata drift while syncLinearIssues upserts values. ADO sync/resolution owns revision-test writes. Jira mappings have no Linear ownership preview. This feature reuses SDK conflict decisions and existing Linear projections, isolates local reads, and adds observational context only. Installed pinned SDK is 2026.10.20; current registry CLI is 2026.10.27, with no dependency bump planned."
  "2026-10-27T09:24:04.444Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked: SDK threeWayFieldConflict and complete SDK reads cover core comparison and acquisition. Linear negotiateLinearSchema detects metadata drift; syncLinearIssues upserts values. ADO sync/resolution owns revision-test writes; Jira has no Linear ownership preview. This adds observational context only. Pinned SDK is 2026.10.20; registry CLI is 2026.10.27, with no pin bump planned."
  "2026-10-27T09:30:26.778Z",codex-agent,"Implemented read-only ownership preview with isolated SDK complete reads, SDK canonicalDocument normalization, role-based status mapping and existing due-date projection. No create/update/apply path or package journal is introduced. Baselines are explicit operator-acknowledged observation artifacts, scoped by item/provider identity and mapping. Invalid/duplicate field records fail alone as unknown. Correction to overlap note: threeWayFieldConflict is ADO package logic, not a core SDK export. Targeted tests caught timestamp-versus-date drift; both sides now use the existing export-date projection."
  "2026-10-27T09:37:41.613Z",codex-agent,"Public immutable-copy validation: 109 real items; original unlinked selection refused before network (0 requests). A separately declared one-item synthetic overlay produced disjoint local/provider edits (1/1), 0 unknowns, 1 same-field conflict, 6 total read requests, and a 2542-byte JSON receipt. Source hashes unchanged during previews; live Linear is not claimed. Behavioral revert proof: replacing only the new classification with two-way equality failed the known-bases regression (expected 8 unknown fields, observed 0); source restored."
  "2026-10-27T09:47:17.410Z",codex-agent,"Boundary checks passed individually: 4 initial targeted tests, 2 custom-status/isolation tests, and installed-host-link regression. Combined linked-test run hit its 120-second runner timeout under host contention after 2 passing tests; no assertion failure occurred and it is missing full evidence, not approval. Full release gates remain delegated to npm/Bun CI at unchanged thresholds. Inherited atomic import replay probe confirmed same transaction/recovered=true despite a newer differing SDK target; recorded separately as pm-linear-atomic-replay-revision. Ownership preview has no write/recovery path."
  "2026-10-27T09:54:28.284Z",codex-agent,"Linked tests rerun with explicit 600-second timeout: 7 tests passed, 0 failed, in 88 seconds. Separate prototype-shaped key test passed; reverting only parseStatusMap own-property insertion made it fail, then source was restored. Source classification revert likewise failed the known-bases regression. Model test contains 500 seeded sequences and is included in CI; local long attempt was canceled under shared-host contention and is not counted as passed. No dedicated lint script exists; typecheck, test typecheck, docstring gate and diff check passed."
  "2026-10-27T09:55:13.927Z",codex-agent,"Packed acceptance passed all 5 isolated host modes: project-local npm, npm global symlink, Bun global, npx and bunx; each made 2 provider reads and returned all 8 unknown fields without a baseline. Supported lazy SDK loading uses host-installed SDK linkage, never argv/which/symlink path inference. Exact report: docs/field-ownership-packed.json. Installed runtime SDK links are excluded from source data copies; foreign item symlinks still refuse. Ready for review with full npm/Bun CI gate evidence pending; inherited replay follow-up remains open."
  "2026-10-27T10:03:18.303Z",codex-agent,"CI run 40484745175 is queued with no gate counts. Reviewed the seeded reference model while waiting: omitted assignee/deadline values now replace mapped fields rather than inheriting current local values, and provider replay sequences include null deadlines. A temporary 20-sequence diagnostic sample passed; this does not replace the required 500-sequence release suite. Production code is unchanged by this oracle correction."
  "2026-10-27T10:21:18.975Z",codex-agent,"Release-gate evidence remains pending: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/actions/runs/40485647905 at source/test head e469b45 has npm, Bun and both Node jobs queued; no full-suite pass counts are available. The first-push CI wait is capped at 30 minutes by the queue rules. Local strict health exits 1 with the same finding classes/severities as an isolated origin/main copy: extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew (gate-failing) and provenance_value_domain_invalid (advisory), already tracked by pm-linear-bzam and pm-linear-jloc. Both changed history streams preserve their main prefixes. Additional overlap verification inspected all 377 public SDK declaration files in CLI 2026.10.26; its pure document/JSON merge helpers have preferred-side/collection merge semantics and are not used as a Linear write or ownership guarantee. Production code remains unchanged since 5f09574; 500-sequence property and full npm/Bun gate evidence must be obtained in CI. PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/pull/183. Items remain open and the feature claim is released."
  "2026-10-27T10:30:17.718Z",codex-agent,"Final test typecheck caught a declaration-only issue in the corrected reference model: Object.fromEntries erased required SDK metadata fields from its inferred type. The model now explicitly carries type, created_at and updated_at from SDK read-back; runtime values are unchanged. npm run build:test now passes at the corrected test source. CI remained queued through the 30-minute wait cap, with 0 of 2 full release gates completed and no pass counts. Superseded queued runs will be canceled; the PR links the latest head checks. Production code remains unchanged, items are unclosed, and the feature claim remains released."
  "2026-10-27T10:49:34.672Z",codex-agent,"Re-review round 1: all four findings accepted. General classes: one source of truth for provider-to-local mapping; provider schemas match nullable/optional API domains; validate entire baseline including duplicate identities before trusting any row; validate GraphQL envelopes before dereferencing. Merged the newer main release first. Audit covers all request consumers, schema/thread/closure/import/export commands, SDK and CLI render paths, baseline ingestion and packed non-git consumers. Will add adversarial/property coverage and per-class behavioral revert proofs, then run serial npm/Bun full gates at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-27T12:03:24.777Z",codex-agent,"Re-review fixes close four classes: preview now calls the import mapper and SDK canonicalizer; import/ownership share nullable issue schemas; the entire baseline is validated before any authority is returned; every HTTP consumer validates the envelope before dereference and preserves typed source_invalid field diagnostics through JSON/TOON dispatch. The package-wide lookup audit also hardened prototype-shaped mapping keys and skips ambiguous current Linear identities in both writers. Behavioral reverts fail for independent status mapping (conflict witness), nullable cycle schema (valid response refused), malformed duplicate baseline handling (unknown_base assertion), unchecked envelopes (typed-refusal assertion), and inherited-property lookup (mapping assertion). Restored production source after each revert; no tests weakened. Focused shared dispatch/preflight/container tests: 3 passed; typecheck, test typecheck and 88-declaration docstring gate passed. Full serial npm/Bun gates and refreshed packed/public-copy evidence follow."
  "2026-10-27T12:16:31.669Z",codex-agent,"Focused re-review linked test run passed 10/10 (328 seconds), including all-field malformed duplicate permutations, nullable/omitted provider objects, SDK/CLI consumers and preflight. Additional focused legacy empty-body/tag application and malformed create/update acknowledgements passed 2/2; the latter report write_unconfirmed instead of confirming malformed responses. A temporary 20-sequence diagnostic against the real atomic dry-run oracle passed; permanent model remains 500 sequences. Broader network/schema run had 91/92 pass with one old viewer-message expectation; that expectation now requires the stronger source_invalid field diagnostic, and its focused rerun passed. Public immutable-copy refresh: 109 items; original selection 0 requests; one-item synthetic overlay, 8 fields, 6 reads, 2542 JSON bytes, disjoint 1/1 and 1 same-field conflict, hashes unchanged. Starting serial full npm/Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds with one test worker."
  "2026-10-27T12:23:20.989Z",codex-agent,"Expanded packed dispatch caught an inherited alias registration mismatch: linear-sync import handled all import options but advertised only schema-version, so the strict host parser rejected team/atomic/dry-run before the handler. Fixed the class by sharing one complete flag definition across both import aliases. Registry regression passes; reverting that definition in an isolated source copy fails the SDK flag assertion. Additional isolated behavioral reverts proved the real importer status projection, empty legacy update fields and import-page container validation (all fail expected assertions). Earlier full npm attempt was stopped early to include this production fix; it is not counted as a gate pass. Restarting unchanged serial npm/Bun gates after the focused registry pass; expanded five-mode packed acceptance is rerunning."
  "2026-10-27T12:47:19.345Z",codex-agent,"Expanded packed acceptance passed 5/5: project-local, npm global, Bun global, npx and bunx. Every mode used the pinned 2026.10.20 host SDK with package 2026.10.27, accepted nullable cycles, reported the status conflict, quarantined malformed duplicate baselines and preserved source_invalid/field/exit 2 in JSON and TOON across seven provider command surfaces. Each mode made 23 read requests, covered 14 source-refusal dispatches and emitted a 3221-byte host JSON receipt; no provider mutation request was sent. Report: docs/field-ownership-packed.json. Full npm gate remains active on its 10,001-item corpus test; no failure reported so far."
